{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera","id":1538770,"title":"Failures of the fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-17T11:02:35-07:00","id":1538770,"title":"Failures of the fera","content":"It's a common trope in the game that garou fucked it up really hard with the fera during the war of rage. The world would have been different if that didn't happen, garou must made amends and so on and so on. <br /> <br /> Howether after thinking about it and reading the breed books. Ir has come to my attention that the other fera are pretty much, in their awfullness, massively responsible in the whole mess. Not in the war of rage per se (except the nagah and ananasi) but in the long aftermath. <br /> <br /> So bear with me as I go to the unspoken wall of shape for the other shapeshifter. <br /> <br /> By that I mean specifically their specific failure to accomplish the task given to them, either by flaws or misplaced ideology <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> For a start, just a common failure of everyone<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe war of rage happened during human prehistory. When exactly is unknown, bit at least 10000 years in the past. <br /> <br /> That's a loooooong time to have lost. And yet the fera still act as if they just lost in term of numbers and uneffectiveness. <br /> <br /> Now in non specific order<br /> <br /> Bastet:<br /> Supposed to seek secrets (at least that's what they think, it's said they have not been given a direct task, an ironic gaillure for secret seekers to not have found their own purpose). <br /> Hyper individualistic and yet divided by a tribalism that makes garou inter tribal issues looks like neighbor's disputes (not helped by the fact their tribal lines are inborn rather than chose) and makes any chance of cohesive action impossible. <br /> Seekers of secrets for aeons yet does not put them to use to help Gaia in general, everyone seeks secrets and it seems to be it. <br /> <br /> Corax:<br /> The least awful at their job with the ananasi. And yet for messengers, one wonder what they've been doing for all these millenias. Garou and fera aren't anymore connected even by messages after all these times. Same for feras in general or garou with garou. Seriously, what were they doing? <br /> <br /> Ratkin:<br /> 8 billions humans. Do I need to develop? Dudes, your sole goal in life is to maintain populations, especially the human population, at a certain limit. Their history is one of systematic failure. Even their prized plagues are happening a few times a millenia and with a generally weak effect. <br /> Also they're batshit inside and it's massively their own fault. <br /> <br /> Ananasi: <br /> Typically are doing their job. Their main weakness is not truly a fault of their own, but their utter d\u00e9pendance to their creator. <br /> <br /> Nagah:<br /> Their obsession with the secrecy of their role is damning them at every step. Plus they are awful at their job, seeing the amount of shapeshifter that betrayed Gaia. <br /> Their methods of judgment is also biased, they basically apply everyone's rules to the letter, so the litany for the garou, the law of ananas a for the ananasi, etc, which means they specifically base themselves of laws that even the shifters concerned doubt and interpret. The garou have two auspices who argue about the litany every morning, and many consider their laws to be out of touch. By using them as guideline, the nagah are trapping the others in patterns that might stop them for actually achieve their purpose <br /> <br /> Mokole:<br /> I can understand that it's hard to be trusting when you gain the collective memory of past betrayal, but the point of the mongole is to remember so that others might not repeat the failures of the past. Yet by deliberately isolating themselves, they garantee that dire outcome. Furthermore, their longing for a new time of wondermaking is basically d\u00e9sertion of their role. <br /> <br /> Gurahl: <br /> Same as mokole, while their own grudge is more understandable as with their hibernation they are closer to the massacres of the war of age, they have basically abandoned the world to be without it's needed healers. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bKitsune:<br /> Hard to argue since their purpose is deliberately not yet revealed by luna (Bastets? Get to work for once!), their main flaw is their extreme focalisation on asia, weakening their potential usefulness once their purpose is revealed. <br /> <br /> Nuwisha:<br /> Nearly the worse offenders. Their obsession with practical pranks makes them blind to the suffering caused if their target &quot;don't get it&quot;. <br /> So yes clever boys, you cursed yourself to be limited at 100 members on earth at time I'm until the garou learn to call you with humility. <br /> But what are you gonna do if they don't? <br /> <br /> Rokea:<br /> The cream of the cream of pure stupidity. They have the most simple job of the world:survive. And every tool at their disposal for that. Yet it seems they do everything on lazy mode. They're hostile to other fera although they can help with rokea's survival by eliminating treats. And worst of all, their dogmatic obsession with eliminating the inlanders garantees that they have no knowledge of what transpires out of the sea, which led to the carnage with a specific atomic testing. <br /> <br /> <br /> And I originally didn't wanted to talk about the lost breed, as they're not really awful, the grondr and the apis were just in the way, but the camazotz existed until a few centuries ago. <br /> <br /> So Camazotz:<br /> Failed their job even harder than the Corax, plus the extermination is partly on their own hands/wings. For aeon they were trapped on the cycle of Bat going from gaian half to wyrm half, allowing their fallen brethren to take prominence during the darker period of the cycle. <br /> And more than 10 000 years should have been enough to deal with it. For ears if Gaia, they forgot to even try to talk to others about the issue. Hell, according to apocalyptic records, the garou succeeded in healing bat. So the camazotz have no excuses. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T18:28:19-07:00","id":1538808,"title":"","content":"I think your comments speak to a truth of the setting. This is how I handle it in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> 1) There was no such thing as a &quot;War of Rage&quot;. Like the Hundred Years War, it is a concept that historians created to better explain the event or era in retrospect. At the time those events occurred, nobody thought of them as a single struggle. That's why the tribes and Fera all have different ideas about who started it and why. They are actually talking about different events centuries and thousands of miles apart which were later combined into one story. Indeed, I don't think Stone Age peoples could even conceive of &quot;war&quot; as a distinct concept. Fighting and killing one another over territory and resources is simply what people did back then, the Garou and Fera were not exceptions.<br /> <br /> 2) While the Garou clearly kicked a lot of ass in their own territory (the natural range of the wolf), the idea that they somehow invaded areas where wolves did not exist to kill other Changing Breeds there does not make much sense to me. Killing a bunch of Gurahl in Europe and northern Asia I can buy. But killing the Ratkin in southeast Asia? No, but I could see the local Bastet doing that.<br /> <br /> 3) The concept of the War of Rage was probably invented by Garou Galliards centuries after its end in order to glorify the accomplishments of the Garou, but once invented the concept spread elsewhere. The Garou and the Changing Breeds as a whole retain a lot of archaic cultural features, and traditionalists still come from a Shame culture. Guilt cultures develop a lot longer on. It was the Children of Gaia who probably first took the concept of the War of Rage and turned it into something the Garou shouldn't have done. Then as the cultural collapse of the Changing Breeds accelerated in the twentieth century and modern notions of guilt culture spread, it's turned into this albatross that hangs around the Garou and an excuse for the Changing Breeds for their own failures. People like to blame other people.<br /> <br /> 4) None of the Changing Breeds exist for a specific reason like &quot;fighting&quot;, &quot;spying&quot;, &quot;sending messages&quot;, and so on. Those are just myths the Changing Breeds like to talk about themselves in order to provide meaning and purpose to their own people. Those myths express just enough truth about their kind that it makes sense on a superficial level, but they fall apart once you think about it.<br /> <br /> That is what I determined actually happened in my chronicles' history as an ST. That doesn't mean I present it to the players as the truth. NPCs have their own opinions, but mostly repeat the standard lore. But some dissent, and some even get close to the truth. PCs can believe whatever they want.<br /> <br /> I sometimes try to sneak in arguments as a PC in certain games along these lines, but not too much because some players and STs get really confused, angered, or defensive if other PCs depart too much from the books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T19:17:37-07:00","id":1538809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1538808#post1538808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your comments speak to a truth of the setting. This is how I handle it in my chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly agree with all of this! I don't really see the War of Rage as a singular event but rather a series of skirmishes and massacres spanning over a long period of time, with no clear beginning or end. In WtE, we don't list a second War of Rage, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#274e13\"><i>Age of Tragedy: The War of Rage</i></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Bookletter 1911\">Many conflicts and disputes plagued the history of the Gaians from the very beginning, and some have been dubbed as part of the greater war. The fact remains that<b> it was a long-brewing problem that only kept escalating</b>. Galliards ken the earliest skirmishes began as the first human civilizations rose to power. A time when killi ruled and guided mankind openly, some were seen as gods by their kin. And with those cultures and their territories, new tensions arose. The war is better understood as a collection of smaller disputes that escalated to much larger bloodshed. The Garou felt betrayed and disrespected by other shapeshifters, accusing them of failing their duties to Gaia or outright corruption.<br /> <br /> In the end, through failed diplomacy and hubris, the Garou went on a massacre that lasted generations.</span></span>\u200b <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Bookletter 1911\">Believing in their own superiority, they began systematically hunting down other breeds. </span></span><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Bookletter 1911\"><b>Some killi were driven to extinction by the conflict, lost forever to time and legend. Some still struggled to recover their populations, while a few began hunting each other.</b> Some escaped the conflict by hiding in the darkest corners of the Earth, on faraway lands, or even in the Umbral depths. <b>How it ended depends on which killi you speak to, but the open wounds of this conflict persist to this day.</b></span></span> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T02:29:21-07:00","id":1538821,"title":"","content":"If your looking for specific responsibilities:-<br /> <br /> - Simba ( Not All Simba!) are responsible for the decimation and forced relocation of the Ajaba and various other African Nightfolk..<br /> - Nagah are plausibly responsible for the first shots in the War of Rage.......Ananasi are.....possibly.....much more responsible if certain sources are to be believed. Ananasi also wiped out entire species of other Arthropod shifters.<br /> -Rokea wiped out shifter servants of Qyrl.......whether before or after the Wyrm aspect was corrupted isn't stated.<br /> - Mokole way back in the day of drachid forms and Dragon Kings were extremely ruthless in protecting their hedgemony leading to a number of other Nightfolk being exterminated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T11:23:31-07:00","id":1538848,"title":"","content":"In writing the Players Guides for Savage Age, this was one topic that we felt was absolutely necessary to be addressed. So each Breed had their failures that contributed/exacerbated the War of Rage, rather than just blaming the Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T11:40:56-07:00","id":1538850,"title":"","content":"Yep, let's add one that I forgot. I may have spoke too soon about the Ananasi.<br /> Following the kidnapping of their queen by the wyrm, the breed was basically blackmailed by the wyrm to do it's bidding. <br /> Their were cut from their maker for millenia, until they made a cunning plan: trick the garou into entering malfeas and attack the protection/prison of the queen, allowing her voice to reach again her children. <br /> <br /> Excuse me, it took them MILLENIAS to think of tricking the murder hobos of the shifters to go seek their queen? <br /> <br /> I think the big problem for the stories of both garous and feras is the notion of big time. Having their history spread across such a large span of time with so little action makes them all look profoundly incompetent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T11:42:51-07:00","id":1538851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1538808#post1538808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your comments speak to a truth of the setting. This is how I handle it in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> 1) There was no such thing as a &quot;War of Rage&quot;. Like the Hundred Years War, it is a concept that historians created to better explain the event or era in retrospect. At the time those events occurred, nobody thought of them as a single struggle. That's why the tribes and Fera all have different ideas about who started it and why. They are actually talking about different events centuries and thousands of miles apart which were later combined into one story. Indeed, I don't think Stone Age peoples could even conceive of &quot;war&quot; as a distinct concept. Fighting and killing one another over territory and resources is simply what people did back then, the Garou and Fera were not exceptions.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, the war of rage always present a coherency me issue. The garou apparently united to kill their fellow feras, in a very successful way, and that before any garou nation was made. <br /> <br /> And you want me to believe that then garou failed to made such unions against vampires and other ennemies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T13:44:53-07:00","id":1538857,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree about the fact that it's more a very long and bloody era where everyone was guilty. The werewolf just took the cherry on the cake as they are so good at killing stuff and work as a group, when most fera are mostly solo-ish players.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the garou 'making' the war of Rage as a thing to glorify themselves, and it came back to bite them in the ass. Though, in this option, shouldn't the mokole know it's far from the truth ? At least the ones with a strong mnesis ? Why would they let this false idea be so widespread when they could be the spark that reunite the shapeshifters to get together for Ga\u00efa ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T15:52:25-07:00","id":1538872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1538857#post1538857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to agree about the fact that it's more a very long and bloody era where everyone was guilty. The werewolf just took the cherry on the cake as they are so good at killing stuff and work as a group, when most fera are mostly solo-ish players.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the garou 'making' the war of Rage as a thing to glorify themselves, and it came back to bite them in the ass. Though, in this option, shouldn't the mokole know it's far from the truth ? At least the ones with a strong mnesis ? Why would they let this false idea be so widespread when they could be the spark that reunite the shapeshifters to get together for Ga\u00efa ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose because they know how aggressive the Garou nation can be towards those who aren't part of them, especially the Mokole, who according to some are very reminiscent of Wyrm creatures. Even if that weren't the case, I think it's very difficult for them to convince Garou of this, I mean their argument are that they remember through an ability that only they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T16:22:35-07:00","id":1538875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera#post1538770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a common trope in the game that garou fucked it up really hard with the fera during the war of rage. The world would have been different if that didn't happen, garou must made amends and so on and so on.<br /> <br /> Howether after thinking about it and reading the breed books. Ir has come to my attention that the other fera are pretty much, in their awfullness, massively responsible in the whole mess. Not in the war of rage per se (except the nagah and ananasi) but in the long aftermath.<br /> <br /> So bear with me as I go to the unspoken wall of shape for the other shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> By that I mean specifically their specific failure to accomplish the task given to them, either by flaws or misplaced ideology<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> For a start, just a common failure of everyone<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe war of rage happened during human prehistory. When exactly is unknown, bit at least 10000 years in the past.<br /> <br /> That's a loooooong time to have lost. And yet the fera still act as if they just lost in term of numbers and uneffectiveness.<br /> <br /> Now in non specific order<br /> <br /> Bastet:<br /> Supposed to seek secrets (at least that's what they think, it's said they have not been given a direct task, an ironic gaillure for secret seekers to not have found their own purpose).<br /> Hyper individualistic and yet divided by a tribalism that makes garou inter tribal issues looks like neighbor's disputes (not helped by the fact their tribal lines are inborn rather than chose) and makes any chance of cohesive action impossible.<br /> Seekers of secrets for aeons yet does not put them to use to help Gaia in general, everyone seeks secrets and it seems to be it.<br /> <br /> Corax:<br /> The least awful at their job with the ananasi. And yet for messengers, one wonder what they've been doing for all these millenias. Garou and fera aren't anymore connected even by messages after all these times. Same for feras in general or garou with garou. Seriously, what were they doing?<br /> <br /> Ratkin:<br /> 8 billions humans. Do I need to develop? Dudes, your sole goal in life is to maintain populations, especially the human population, at a certain limit. Their history is one of systematic failure. Even their prized plagues are happening a few times a millenia and with a generally weak effect.<br /> Also they're batshit inside and it's massively their own fault.<br /> <br /> Ananasi:<br /> Typically are doing their job. Their main weakness is not truly a fault of their own, but their utter d\u00e9pendance to their creator.<br /> <br /> Nagah:<br /> Their obsession with the secrecy of their role is damning them at every step. Plus they are awful at their job, seeing the amount of shapeshifter that betrayed Gaia.<br /> Their methods of judgment is also biased, they basically apply everyone's rules to the letter, so the litany for the garou, the law of ananas a for the ananasi, etc, which means they specifically base themselves of laws that even the shifters concerned doubt and interpret. The garou have two auspices who argue about the litany every morning, and many consider their laws to be out of touch. By using them as guideline, the nagah are trapping the others in patterns that might stop them for actually achieve their purpose<br /> <br /> Mokole:<br /> I can understand that it's hard to be trusting when you gain the collective memory of past betrayal, but the point of the mongole is to remember so that others might not repeat the failures of the past. Yet by deliberately isolating themselves, they garantee that dire outcome. Furthermore, their longing for a new time of wondermaking is basically d\u00e9sertion of their role.<br /> <br /> Gurahl:<br /> Same as mokole, while their own grudge is more understandable as with their hibernation they are closer to the massacres of the war of age, they have basically abandoned the world to be without it's needed healers.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bKitsune:<br /> Hard to argue since their purpose is deliberately not yet revealed by luna (Bastets? Get to work for once!), their main flaw is their extreme focalisation on asia, weakening their potential usefulness once their purpose is revealed.<br /> <br /> Nuwisha:<br /> Nearly the worse offenders. Their obsession with practical pranks makes them blind to the suffering caused if their target &quot;don't get it&quot;.<br /> So yes clever boys, you cursed yourself to be limited at 100 members on earth at time I'm until the garou learn to call you with humility.<br /> But what are you gonna do if they don't?<br /> <br /> Rokea:<br /> The cream of the cream of pure stupidity. They have the most simple job of the world:survive. And every tool at their disposal for that. Yet it seems they do everything on lazy mode. They're hostile to other fera although they can help with rokea's survival by eliminating treats. And worst of all, their dogmatic obsession with eliminating the inlanders garantees that they have no knowledge of what transpires out of the sea, which led to the carnage with a specific atomic testing.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, based on what I know about each species, and making it clear that I'm not an expert, what I understood was the following:<br /> <br /> Corax: They work by transmitting information, obviously, and they collect everything, after all you never know what might be useful. As for what they do to help other species, they select the relevant information and pass it on to whoever needs it, when they need it, I mean, they are not going to send information from a Wyrm or BSD hideout to a pack if they doesn't believe they can do something useful instead of killing themselves acting like heroes.<br /> <br /> Bastet: I admit that these leave me a little lost, in their book it mentions that the feline tricked Gaia into giving him the power to transform into a human and when he didn't fulfill his part of the agreement, she cursed them with the tribe's secrets. I think they just wanted an excuse to include feline races, if you really need a justification, say that they are a species born to keep secrets that others shouldn't know until necessary, or that Corax are more like a extensive network of information and the Bastet are of something deeper, more intimate and hidden.<br /> <br /> Mokole: If I understand correctly, their idea is that for them to remember, they need to survive, hence the isolation and from what I understand, they are much closer to extinction than other species.<br /> <br /> Rokea: Their case is complicated, I think that to survive they want to keep everything constant and that's why they kill invaders and choose not to cooperate, it may not be the most appropriate, but it's a reasoning that makes sense.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T09:43:15-08:00","id":1557420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera#post1538770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> For a start, just a common failure of everyone<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe war of rage happened during human prehistory. When exactly is unknown, bit at least 10000 years in the past.<br /> <br /> That's a loooooong time to have lost. And yet the fera still act as if they just lost in term of numbers and uneffectiveness.<br /> <br /> Now in non specific order<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Fera don't exactly have a say in how frequently they reproduce. All they can do is pop out a kid, and hope that Gaia sees fit to activate their Changing Seed at some point in the future.<br /> <br /> The Ratkin were actually DOING A VERY GOOD JOB around this time. Their plagues were functioning as intended, then the Garou barged in and told them they weren't as efficient as they wanted them to be, so they fucked it up. The Ratkin are insane, because being insane is the only way they can continue to fulfill their purpose. They had humanity's numbers at a manageable rate. But now they're so massive, that even a nation wide epidemic may as well be a drop in the bucket.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T18:29:06-08:00","id":1557490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1557420#post1557420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Fera don't exactly have a say in how frequently they reproduce. All they can do is pop out a kid, and hope that Gaia sees fit to activate their Changing Seed at some point in the future.<br /> <br /> The Ratkin were actually DOING A VERY GOOD JOB around this time. Their plagues were functioning as intended, then the Garou barged in and told them they weren't as efficient as they wanted them to be, so they fucked it up. The Ratkin are insane, because being insane is the only way they can continue to fulfill their purpose. They had humanity's numbers at a manageable rate. But now they're so massive, that even a nation wide epidemic may as well be a drop in the bucket.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Their method of reproduction, except corax and camazotz, are the same as the garou. Have lot sof children with humans/respective animals. Favor kinfolk partners to maximise chances of having fera children. <br /> <br /> <br /> To assume they can only hope Gaia &quot;activate&quot; their offsprings imply Gaia deliberatly kept the fera's population lower than the garou, which run counter to everything we're told about how the lack of fera led to the current nightmarish situation. <br /> <br /> <br /> So the point stand, the wars of rage happened in prehistory. They had dozens of millenia to have lots of kids, ergo favorising the rise in their own number, and repeat the process until lrea H pre war of rage numbers. <br /> <br /> <br /> That's even worse for corax and camazotz, which reproduce by choosing a young human/crow/bat to prepare as a fera. They have direct control on their numbers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I repeat my previous point on the ratkin. The wars of rage ended before written history. They've had dozens of millenia to use plague to reduce human populations. It's not after the war that humanity reached the billions, but in the last centuries. <br /> <br /> You point out their madness as a reaction to the difficulty of their duty, but honestly, being mad doesn't help them. On the contrary, rationality would have led them to move toward engineered plagues with Weaver tools. They could create diseases making large swath of the population infertile, forcing a massive drop in population replacement. But they'd rather use the same tactics that didnt' work for millenia, ergo why they failed at their duty<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T01:01:01-08:00","id":1557496,"title":"","content":"Reproduction is a strange thing in WW<br /> But suprisingly streamlined<br /> <br /> &quot;Genetics isn't an exact science, but the mating of werewolves and Kinfolk produces roughly 90% Kinfolk and 10% Garou offspring. The mating of two Kinfolk changes the numbers to 50% Kinfolk and 1% Garou, with the remainder of children being plain folks. Kin who mate with normal mortals usually bear non-Kin children, though certain factions among the Children of Gaia have a highly secretive rite that can alter this outcome. The Background Pure Breed on the part of either Kinfolk or Garou improves these statistics somewhat.&quot; - Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, pp 13<br /> <br /> &quot;Pure Breed [possessed by kinfolk] also figures quietly into the chances for conceiving a garou child. For every level of this Background you purchase, the chance of producing a full Garou offspring with a werewolf partner increases 5%. (Note: The Garou's Pure Breed, if any, does NOT figure into the odds.)&quot; - Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, pp 51<br /> <br /> &quot;In cases of Kin/Kin pairings, the chance for werewolf offspring increases by 1% for every dot of Pure Breed.&quot; - Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, pp 51<br /> <br /> &quot;...if two Shapeshifters of Different Breeds conceive a child, the child has a 10% chance to be a shapeshifter of the father's kind, a 10% chance to be a shapeshifter of the mother's kind, and an 80% chance to be a normal kin to either. If the mother is lupus, feline or whatever, however, any children will be normal Kin to her Changing Breed or shapeshifters like herself - a lupus cannot give birth to a Khan or to tiger cubs.&quot; - Werewolf Players Guide (2nd Edition), pp 190<br /> <br /> &quot;In no cases can a shapeshifter be of two separate Changing Breeds; a Garou with Bastet blood is simply Kin to the Bastet and nothing more. There isn't room for two shapeshifter souls in one body.&quot; - Werewolf Players Guide (2nd Edition), pp 190<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T01:03:00-08:00","id":1557497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1557490#post1557490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You point out their madness as a reaction to the difficulty of their duty, but honestly, being mad doesn't help them. On the contrary, rationality would have led them to move toward engineered plagues with Weaver tools. They could create diseases making large swath of the population infertile, forcing a massive drop in population replacement. But they'd rather use the same tactics that didnt' work for millenia, ergo why they failed at their duty<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only ones stupid enough to think they can beat Weaver at their own game are the Glasswalkers. Who, last I checked, were well on their way to becoming mass Drones, after they started loading their bodies up with Technocrat Cybernetics. Even the Ananasi realize that Weaver has completely lost their mind, and are trying to replace it with Queen Ananasa.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember, the Black Plague wiped out 2/3 of Europe, and only ended because it killed faster than it could spread. Humanity didn't develop a counter measure for it, they just became too thinned out for it to reach a new host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T03:03:19-08:00","id":1557500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1557497#post1557497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only ones stupid enough to think they can beat Weaver at their own game are the Glasswalkers. Who, last I checked, were well on their way to becoming mass Drones, after they started loading their bodies up with Technocrat Cybernetics. Even the Ananasi realize that Weaver has completely lost their mind, and are trying to replace it with Queen Ananasa.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember, the Black Plague wiped out 2/3 of Europe, and only ended because it killed faster than it could spread. Humanity didn't develop a counter measure for it, they just became too thinned out for it to reach a new host.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Who spoke of serving the Weaver? This is about using her tools. Which most of homid garou are doing newaday, and they aren't on their way to be home mass drones. neither are glass walkers, I'm not sure what you're referencing with Technocrat tech, but with the exception of that one forced cyborg lupus in rage across Australia, there's hardly any such used in the tribe, you may be thinking of the cyber dogs camp, which is an outlier.<br /> <br /> Same for ananasi, yes they know the Weaver is mad (the same as 99% of every garou/fera know she went mad, it's basically cosmology 101 for every recently first changed pup) but they use her tools and have a third of their dsepcies dedicated to acting on the behalf of order. <br /> <br /> <br /> Ratkin wouldn't magically became drones by using gene sequencing in order to sterilise vast swaths of the human population. <br /> <br /> <br /> To the point of the black death, it too shows the inadequacies of Ratkin. Yes it wiped out 2/3 or Europe. Yet it only took between 150-200 years approximately to reach back pre plague numbers of the population. And centuries later, the population on the continent is three quarters of a billion. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T03:22:53-08:00","id":1557501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1557500#post1557500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Who spoke of serving the Weaver? This is about using her tools. Which most of homid garou are doing newaday, and they aren't on their way to be home mass drones. neither are glass walkers, I'm not sure what you're referencing with Technocrat tech, but with the exception of that one forced cyborg lupus in rage across Australia, there's hardly any such used in the tribe, you may be thinking of the cyber dogs camp, which is an outlier.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was my understanding the Glass Walkers infiltrated the Technocracy, and not only managed to steal a bunch of their technology, but also blackmailed them into backing down when they were preparing to launch an attack. Basically warning them that they knew the identities and locations of all their agents, and could easily retaliate if necessary.<br /> <br /> So the Glass Walker tribe has access to stuff like cybernetic implants and plasma guns. Which they foolishly believe they can repurpose to serve the spirit of Gaia, rather than Weaver..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-12-2026, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T11:46:25-08:00","id":1557521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1557501#post1557501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was my understanding the Glass Walkers infiltrated the Technocracy, and not only managed to steal a bunch of their technology, but also blackmailed them into backing down when they were preparing to launch an attack. Basically warning them that they knew the identities and locations of all their agents, and could easily retaliate if necessary.<br /> <br /> So the Glass Walker tribe has access to stuff like cybernetic implants and plasma guns. Which they foolishly believe they can repurpose to serve the spirit of Gaia, rather than Weaver..</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be a headcannon of a game master you played with, but that's not the case in the base setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> The GW and the technocracy have a minuscule ammount of contact, a classic case of the forced separation of the splats in the wod.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, the scenario you described couldnt' happen. Technocrats are mages, no matter how much they dislike the term, the crushing majority of heir tech is only usable by pages. The glass walkers couldn't use it.<br /> <br /> GW tech is mainly the result of their house of technological development, techno fetishes develloped over centuries of practice and/or spirit tech taken from the cyberealms or tech inspired by exploring the dreams of the sleeping incarnate of technology.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, that's how the whole cybernetic implant thing came about. It was a pack of glass walkers, the cyber dogs, who went through extended journey into the cyber realm to get spiritual cynernetics adapted to garou morphology, a practice which turned into a whole camp. Camp which was purged as they were doing terrible experiments on lupus in their quest to upgrade Gaia.<br /> <br /> The only time we know of where the GW and the technocracy had any exchange of knowledge is in the progenitor revised convention book, where the progenitor received an offer from the GW, they'd stop capturing garou for their research, and the tribe offer in exchange a sharing of data on garojmu's biology. But even that was in the domain of the potential as the leaders of the progenitor &quot;has yet to make a decision on that proposal&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 01-12-2026, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T14:47:18-07:00","id":1558756,"title":"","content":"The game is Were<b>wolf</b>, ergo, the Garou were right. The Fera (minus the Kitsune, who didn't exist yet) were all miserable, useless failures, so Gaia put the Garou into the field to whip the others into shape. They refused to fall in line because of pride and (in most cases) Rage. When they disobeyed the Garou, they disobeyed Gaia, and they got what was coming to them; it's really as simple as that.<br /> <br /> I would only append one thing saying that the stupid party in this has always been Gaia. Even before trying to fix things with the Garou, she created creatures that have Rage (their gift from the Wyrm), and which, Rage or no Rage, are hostile to one another in nature. Keeping in mind that nature is Gaia's domain, she was seriously idiotic to expect them to work together at all, so while I stand on the Fera failing, and the Garou being right to put them down for their betrayal, Gaia is the real guilty party in this, just by virtue of sheer incompetence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","user":"Lord Vil","date":". 03-09-2026, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpa