ling, and the Garou being right to put them down for their betrayal, Gaia is the real guilty party in this, just by virtue of sheer incompetence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just to be clear, is that a troll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 03-11-2026, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T18:34:27-07:00","id":1558813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558756#post1558756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The game is Were<b>wolf</b>, ergo, the Garou were right. The Fera (minus the Kitsune, who didn't exist yet) were all miserable, useless failures, so Gaia put the Garou into the field to whip the others into shape. They refused to fall in line because of pride and (in most cases) Rage. When they disobeyed the Garou, they disobeyed Gaia, and they got what was coming to them; it's really as simple as that.<br /> <br /> I would only append one thing saying that the stupid party in this has always been Gaia. Even before trying to fix things with the Garou, she created creatures that have Rage (their gift from the Wyrm), and which, Rage or no Rage, are hostile to one another in nature. Keeping in mind that nature is Gaia's domain, she was seriously idiotic to expect them to work together at all, so while I stand on the Fera failing, and the Garou being right to put them down for their betrayal, Gaia is the real guilty party in this, just by virtue of sheer incompetence.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't agree with the entire sentiment, this comment does have some good ideas, and since we are talking about the failures of the Fera in this thread, I will focus on that to not derail it. While there was no way, Changing Breed kind was seen as useless in Gaia's eyes. (The Ratkin were good at their job canonically until the Impergium [just ignore East Asia], The Rokea didn't really care about Betweeners until recently with the Turna'a Massacre, The Ajaba did actually perform their jobs as Cullers well, so well that Black Tooth performed a genocide against them).<br /> <br /> I do agree that Garou were born to lead the Changing Breeds through the apocalypse, they were created for combat, they are spread via the auspices to better understand different tasks (Theurges helping Bastet or Philodoxes aiding Gurahl), while they are masters of combat and violence, they are made to relate and provide aid to the other Changing Breeds as they lead them to aggressive action against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Garou lost that, by being insane braggards who killed three Changing Breeds, aggravated the others, and bumbled around within themselves to the extent that they killed three tribes. I can understand why no one wants them to lead... I for one vote for an Ajaba-led Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29035-ghostcat","name":"Ghostcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T04:08:44-07:00","id":1558818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558756#post1558756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The game is Were<b>wolf</b>, ergo, the Garou were right. The Fera (minus the Kitsune, who didn't exist yet) were all miserable, useless failures, so Gaia put the Garou into the field to whip the others into shape. They refused to fall in line because of pride and (in most cases) Rage. When they disobeyed the Garou, they disobeyed Gaia, and they got what was coming to them; it's really as simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gurahl were absolutely right in denying the Garou the secret of resurrection.<br /> <br /> First of all, that ritual is extremely difficult to perform, and has a chance of going horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> Do you trust a society of rage fueled berserkers, many of whom don't exactly have a good relationship with their so called 'kinfolk,' to have the wisdom or patience to use it properly?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558756#post1558756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would only append one thing saying that the stupid party in this has always been Gaia. Even before trying to fix things with the Garou, she created creatures that have Rage (their gift from the Wyrm), and which, Rage or no Rage, are hostile to one another in nature. Keeping in mind that nature is Gaia's domain, she was seriously idiotic to expect them to work together at all, so while I stand on the Fera failing, and the Garou being right to put them down for their betrayal, Gaia is the real guilty party in this, just by virtue of sheer incompetence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is, the Red Talons may be the closest in line with Gaia's will out of any of the tribes.<br /> <br /> There is a lot of evidence which suggests that Gaia may not be the benevolent goddess that the Garou portray her has.<br /> <br /> For one thing, she actually wants to kick humanity back to the Neolithic era and <b>keep them there.</b><br /> <br /> She hates industrialized society, and seeks a return back to a more primal world. One in which humans were little more than hairless apes, instead of the hyper intelligent apex predators they are now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T10:19:15-07:00","id":1558822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558818#post1558818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The funny thing is, the Red Talons may be the closest in line with Gaia's will out of any of the tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's actually certain is that they've kept hold of what it means to be a wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a lot of evidence which suggests that Gaia may not be the benevolent goddess that the Garou portray her has.<br /> <br /> For one thing, she actually wants to kick humanity back to the Neolithic era and <b>keep them there.</b><br /> <br /> She hates industrialized society, and seeks a return back to a more primal world. One in which humans were little more than hairless apes, instead of the hyper intelligent apex predators they are now. </div> </div> </div>There's very little direct portrayal of Gaia at all. What we can glean from the Prophecy of the Phoenix is that the exact way the modern world turned out was not in accord with Her desires, and that's pretty open-ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T15:21:40-07:00","id":1558843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558822#post1558822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's actually certain is that they've kept hold of what it means to be a wolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's very little direct portrayal of Gaia at all. What we can glean from the Prophecy of the Phoenix is that the exact way the modern world turned out was not in accord with Her desires, and that's pretty open-ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even there it's not so much Gaia but Phoenix showing the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T15:28:16-07:00","id":1558844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghostcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558813#post1558813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't agree with the entire sentiment, this comment does have some good ideas, and since we are talking about the failures of the Fera in this thread, I will focus on that to not derail it. While there was no way, Changing Breed kind was seen as useless in Gaia's eyes. (The Ratkin were good at their job canonically until the Impergium [just ignore East Asia], The Rokea didn't really care about Betweeners until recently with the Turna'a Massacre, The Ajaba did actually perform their jobs as Cullers well, so well that Black Tooth performed a genocide against them).<br /> <br /> I do agree that Garou were born to lead the Changing Breeds through the apocalypse, they were created for combat, they are spread via the auspices to better understand different tasks (Theurges helping Bastet or Philodoxes aiding Gurahl), while they are masters of combat and violence, they are made to relate and provide aid to the other Changing Breeds as they lead them to aggressive action against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Garou lost that, by being insane braggards who killed three Changing Breeds, aggravated the others, and bumbled around within themselves to the extent that they killed three tribes. I can understand why no one wants them to lead... I for one vote for an Ajaba-led Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's doubtful the garou were meant to rule. They're too rage fueled to even rule themselves. <br /> <br /> As for an ajaba led Gaia, it would be short lived. The only thing streangre with the attempt by black tooth to genocide there ajaba is that it didn't happen sooner. <br /> <br /> There's no way a bunch of rage fueled species would ever accept that some wfetehyenas decides that they are the reightful judge of whose to die to spare the whole their weakness. <br /> <br /> I mean that's exactly why the nagah always hid their purpose, buy feaer of how the changing breed would react to some snakes claiming to be judge, jury and executioner of their litanies no laws. <br /> <br /> If the ajaba were leading, there reign would be seen as a tyranny, and would only last until as one these rage fueled critter refuse to sere their packmate being killed by self righteous herd thinners. <br /> <br /> Which would also it their credibility on a shaky ground, why would, say, the garou, who applaud glory and sees killing the strongest opponent as a sign of worth value beings whose very motto is killing the weak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T17:03:11-07:00","id":1558845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558844#post1558844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even there it's not so much Gaia but Phoenix showing the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Phoenix doesn't just do that, though, and seemed to have help from outside their specific spiritual purview in showing the future - particularly in communicating that it's how things would turn out, but now how they should turn out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T22:33:46-07:00","id":1558931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558809#post1558809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just to be clear, is that a troll?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not trolling. Look, I personally prefer playing certain of the Fera. At the end of the day, though, the game is WereWOLF. The Garou are the central protagonists, and that's the perspective from which I come at this. <br /> The Garou, being the central figures of the game, should be the only ones who ultimately matter in the long run. It should be so much the case that, if all of the Fera go extinct, and only the Garou stand, the Garou still have that very, very narrow chance of saving Gaia before their doomed species joins the Fera in the void. On the other side of the same coin, if the Garou all become extinct, and the Fera stand, then Gaia's fate should be sealed. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T22:36:40-07:00","id":1558932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558775#post1558775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. I thought that the &quot;The name of the game is WereWOLF!&quot; people had all moved on to Forsaken and abandoned Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer Apocalypse as a game, and the World of Darkness far over Chronicles of Darkness, so much that I have no love for 5th Edition, wherein the developers decided that people who prefer the World of Darkness should get Chronicles of Darkness with a World of Darkness paintjob. To further clarify, I don't dislike the Fera at all. Hell, I prefer playing some of them over playing Garou, buit I understand that they're meant to be second fiddle to the Garou. Shit, if we go back to First Edition, and for as much as I like certain Fera, it should have remained this way: Fera were things to kill and gain Renown for killing, aberrations that didn't have the decency to stay dead in the War of Rage - if you played one in a Werewolf game, you understood that it was to be a short-lived character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T22:57:05-07:00","id":1558933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558932#post1558932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I prefer Apocalypse as a game, and the World of Darkness far over Chronicles of Darkness, so much that I have no love for 5th Edition, wherein the developers decided that people who prefer the World of Darkness should get Chronicles of Darkness with a World of Darkness paintjob.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you'd been paying attention you'd know that this is not, in fact, what happened. What most of WoD5 is, is mostly a bizarre amalgamation of both that somehow manages to avoid what fans of either game wanted almost perfectly. If its patchwork hide is stretched over any bones, they would be of Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To further clarify, I don't dislike the Fera at all. Hell, I prefer playing some of them over playing Garou, buit I understand that they're meant to be second fiddle to the Garou. Shit, if we go back to First Edition, and for as much as I like certain Fera, it should have remained this way: Fera were things to kill and gain Renown for killing, aberrations that didn't have the decency to stay dead in the War of Rage - if you played one in a Werewolf game, you understood that it was to be a short-lived character. </div> </div> </div>And perhaps you'd be better off hanging out with the &quot;3025 only&quot; crowd from BattleTech while you're at it. Really cheerful people, those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-20T11:00:13-07:00","id":1558953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558932#post1558932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I prefer Apocalypse as a game, and the World of Darkness far over Chronicles of Darkness, so much that I have no love for 5th Edition, wherein the developers decided that people who prefer the World of Darkness should get Chronicles of Darkness with a World of Darkness paintjob.</div> </div> </div> </div>World of Darkness was a product that was made in the 90's, by the 90's, for the 90's, and it ended at a suitably appropriate time.<br /> <br /> Trying to resurrect it after 20 years went about as successfully as you might expect.<br /> <br /> By trying to update the game <i>'for the modern audience,'</i> they ended up alienating the older fans while failing to bring in enough new ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree, if you want to play 5th edition, just play Chronicles. Most of what 5th edition is attempting to do was already introduced in Chronicles, except it was done better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T04:21:59-07:00","id":1561926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1558756#post1558756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The game is Were<b>wolf</b>, ergo, the Garou were right.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly wrong.<br /> <br /> One of the main themes of the game is that the closed-mindedness of Elders and previous generations bears a lot of weight in how things turned up.<br /> <br /> Even assuming the Garou as protagonists this theme remains, where PCs that seek to win the Apocalypse War have the challenge of making Garou society overcome a helluva lot of shit.<br /> <br /> So even setting aside that the game is not built to force any particular protagonist and the Fera being right isn't against canon, the game in no way, shape or form ever proposed any of your allegations. Any single one of them. <hr /><br /> No Changing Breed was made to lead the others in anything. And thinking otherwise isn't a Garou problem, it's a Silver Fang problem.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons aren't right and don't know what it means to be a wolf. They don't have the foggiest idea of what it means to be a wolf, as real wolves don't remotely behave as Red Talons unless they're caged for years in conditions similar to a Salvadoran prison with complete strangers.<br /> <br /> W5 is based off V5, that's the end of it. The dev team was directly instructed to work in the same vibes and themes and ignore Werewolf's proposals.<br /> <br /> Just as V20, W20 was an absolute success. And yes, those games are absolutely a 90s thing. That's only a problem if you don't know that, since the 20th Ann edition didn't pretend otherwise. And V5 tried to be a romanticized &quot;those were better times&quot; delirious version of the early 90s, which is not the same thing. Trying to update for a modern audience wasn't the problem, being incompetent at that was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T01:10:43-07:00","id":1562249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1561926#post1561926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Red Talons aren't right and don't know what it means to be a wolf. They don't have the foggiest idea of what it means to be a wolf, as real wolves don't remotely behave as Red Talons unless they're caged for years in conditions similar to a Salvadoran prison with complete strangers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering they were just normal wolves before undergoing the first change, it's understandable that they would try to reject their human half as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Only using their homid form in dire emergencies, and only for as long as absolutely necessary to accomplish their goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T04:11:17-07:00","id":1562251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562249#post1562249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering they were just normal wolves before undergoing the first change, it's understandable that they would try to reject their human half as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Only using their homid form in dire emergencies, and only for as long as absolutely necessary to accomplish their goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do human-born Garou reject their wolf form as much as possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T06:53:04-07:00","id":1562256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562251#post1562251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do human-born Garou reject their wolf form as much as possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but the human-born Garou were already sapient before undergoing the first change.<br /> <br /> Where as the wolf-born were spontaneously blasted with sentience, and then told they had to mingle with human civilization in a war against cosmic forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T10:36:37-07:00","id":1562264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562256#post1562256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but the human-born Garou were already sapient before undergoing the first change.<br /> <br /> Where as the wolf-born were spontaneously blasted with sentience, and then told they had to mingle with human civilization in a war against cosmic forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the wolf-born are consistently described as feeling alienated among wolves before the First Change, precisely because they are sapient (I'd prefer human-like cognition) from the get go.<br /> <br /> No Garou was ever an animal or a human. They are all just Garou since birth. None is suddenly blasted with sapience, the Change is consistently described as a start of self-discovery as they now have the references to understand what they always felt.<br /> <br /> Wolf-born aren't required to mingle with humans, no Garou is. At most they're required to learn the basics to not draw attention. Every Garou is actually expected to avoid humans as much as possible given the whole Rage thing.<br /> <br /> The war against cosmic forces is everyone's problem, no one asked for this.<br /> <br /> You clearly never read what the books have to say about the wolf-born. Or about how they are in each tribe, given that every tribe has them. What the Red Talons do is Red Talon culture, it is as arbitrary as any human culture, and just as misaligned with actual wolf instincts.<br /> <br /> Given, again, that they don't behave like real wolves at all. Never did. They never understood what it is like and never will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T12:40:31-07:00","id":1562269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562264#post1562264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wolf-born aren't required to mingle with humans, no Garou is. <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>They do if they plan to have offspring. Which was a direct commandment that the Bunyip were expected to fulfill, as soon as they became biologically capable of doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562264#post1562264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You clearly never read what the books have to say about the wolf-born. Or about how they are in each tribe, given that every tribe has them. What the Red Talons do is Red Talon culture, it is as arbitrary as any human culture, and just as misaligned with actual wolf instincts.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I was working off the impression that Garou initially grow up believing they are normal until the first change happens. But I guess that's more of a Forsaken thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T13:30:00-07:00","id":1562273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562269#post1562269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do if they plan to have offspring. Which was a direct commandment that the Bunyip were expected to fulfill, as soon as they became biologically capable of doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was working off the impression that Garou initially grow up believing they are normal until the first change happens. But I guess that's more of a Forsaken thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou usually have one night stands, even with Kinfolk. The few who form deeper bonds are playing a dangerous game, and while this is common and not a crime, the Nation definitely doesn't favor such arrangements.<br /> <br /> So even setting aside that they can mate with wolves instead and never touch a human like that, the amount of &quot;mingling&quot; is incredibly limited.<br /> <br /> On the other part: Neurodivergent people also grow up believing we're normal until we get a diagnosis suspicion. You have no reference frame of what a normal human head is like from the inside to say if yours is normal or not. No one has, not even Neurotypicals.<br /> <br /> Just like any Neurodivergent, Garou grow up with all sorts of &quot;invisible differences&quot; they can't clearly point out. They're already, from the crib, something else. But there's a whole world of difference between &quot;I'm not entirely normal&quot; and &quot;I know exactly what I am and it isn't human/wolf&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T13:36:54-07:00","id":1562274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562273#post1562273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou usually have one night stands, even with Kinfolk. The few who form deeper bonds are playing a dangerous game, and while this is common and not a crime, the Nation definitely doesn't favor such arrangements.<br /> <br /> So even setting aside that they can mate with wolves instead and never touch a human like that, the amount of &quot;mingling&quot; is incredibly limited.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was not aware of that. Though it does help shed some light on the Fianna's party animal behavior.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562273#post1562273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other part: Neurodivergent people also grow up believing we're normal until we get a diagnosis suspicion. You have no reference frame of what a normal human head is like from the inside to say if yours is normal or not. No one has, not even Neurotypicals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I grew up thinking I was a literal alien from another planet, because normie society was utterly incomprehensible to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T13:51:55-07:00","id":1562276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562274#post1562274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I grew up thinking I was a literal alien from another planet, because normie society was utterly incomprehensible to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understand the sentiment, but that still wasn't you knowing what you are, it was you thinking something sets you apart, but unable to point out what.<br /> <br /> Garou go through this, exactly. Most won't conclude they're not human, though, and even less that they're from a race of shapeshifting spirit warriors, just like most Autistics just think they're broken or crazy. That's the extent of the &quot;normal&quot; they believe to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T15:31:41-07:00","id":1562283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538770-failures-of-the-fera?p=1562276#post1562276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Understand the sentiment, but that still wasn't you knowing what you are, it was you thinking something sets you apart, but unable to point out what.<br /> <br /> Garou go through this, exactly. Most won't conclude they're not human, though, and even less that they're from a race of shapeshifting spirit warriors, just like most Autistics just think they're broken or crazy. That's the extent of the &quot;normal&quot; they believe to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense now, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I seem to recall there being a part about how a few weeks leading up to the first change, the subject begins to experience mild hallucinations too as they start to becoming more sensitive to the existence of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Though, again, that might have been a Forsaken thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T16:10:54-07:00","id":1562284,"title":"","content":"That may happen. The weeks before the First Change are a whirlwind of sensations. Hallucinations may happen, mood swings, speech problems, growls. You can add lots of symptoms, this is not an easy period.<br /> <br /> Also, they're starting to smell like werewolf to other Garou. IIRC it isn't strong, but combined with the erratic behavior caused by symptoms, it's a fast giveaway of what's happening. Other Garou frequently find Lost Cubs that way, and that's the reason tribeless Garou aren't way more common.<br /> <br /> But then, that's just the finishing line. Their whole life they felt set apart. And that's actually worse on the wolf-born, because their packs are even less equipped to deal with abnormal behavior than human society, and their highly abstract brains have little contact surface with or ability to communicate with other wolves.<br /> <br /> Human society presents to them a very novel thing: animals that speak. They give a cub the tools to communicate across body intuition. A society where a strange person can still find a place, as bad as it may be, a system they can engage through abstract cognition they're built to have.<br /> <br /> Of course, Garou society can do the same, so that's not really necessary. And that's what happens with the Red Talons. They find a Cub during or after First Change and before they find out humans, and introduce to their society. They indoctrinate as much as any other Tribe, they crate stories, theories, symbols.<br /> <br /> In the end, their &quot;wolfness&quot; is performative, and they can't tell the difference. They ascribe to a lot of popular misconceptions about wolves. Not a single one of them really knows or ever knew what being a wolf is really like, they just delude themselves about this (other tribes delude themselves about other things).<br /> <br /> What they can say for sure is where they grew and who's their birth family. And while less equipped to deal with it, wolf packs are still unlikely to leave even the weirdest member behind, so the wolf-born tend to be close to their packs and wish them well. That extremely human attachment is what really feeds the opinions of the Red Talons.<br /> <br /> So, they're not misanthropes because they are wolves. They're misanthropes because they have a humanlike ability to hold grudges and defend ideas fanatically.<br /> <br /> One of the Revised Tribebooks, I think was Wendigo, had a sample character that was a wolf-born who left the forest and the wolves completely, learned to integrate in human society, graduated and works as a librarian. All that with no Garou interference, he was taught the little he knows about werewolves by the spirits (he's Theurge). So that's a wolf-born for your when they're given freedom to think about their situation. Not all of them, but one of them nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}